hten this race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 64 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Greg Murphy (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Eastern North Carolina's 3rd District leans Republican by about six points, and incumbent Greg Murphy is seeking another term with a decisive financial edge: roughly $2.7 million on hand compared with about $74,000 for Democrat Raymond Smith Jr., a state lawmaker who won his party's primary in March. Outside spending against Murphy has been modest, and little has backed Smith.\n\nEvery major race rating, from Cook and Inside Elections to Sabato and the Silver Bulletin, places this at Likely R or better, and prediction markets give Murphy roughly an 86 percent chance of winning. The one available poll, a Democratic-sponsored August survey, showed a surprisingly narrow 3-point contest, and the national climate favors Democrats this cycle. Those factors keep the expected margin in the high single digits rather than double digits, but the combination of incumbency, money, and the district's lean makes Murphy a clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0988, "margin": -7.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0384, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0979, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1036, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0703, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0567, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0798, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0901, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1267, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.114, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1275, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1234, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0732, "margin": -8.5}]}